nineradar.com,0,"NineRadar — After the close, who printed TD Sequential 9 or 13 What finished today: TD Sequential 9 and 13 after the close. Low-9, high-9, US, HK, A-shares, closed-pair review, lock-screen alerts. A count, not advice. NineRadar — After the close, who printed TD Sequential 9 or 13 Skip to content Nine Radar 九转雷达 Today Stocks Scenes The 9 App Store Language English 简体中文 繁體中文 日本語 한국어 After the close Nine Radar Brokers already paint 9. We scan the whole close. A trading app can mark 9 on the symbol you opened. NineRadar answers a different question after the session: who finished a 9 or 13 — across US, HK, China A-shares, and Korea. Then you can replay only finished pairs. A count, not a pick. Get on the App Store Why not just the broker app iOS. Lock-screen 9s, replay of finished pairs. A count, not advice. Today Watchlist Backtest You After the close · US · HK · CN 12 Low-9 9 High-9 — 13 4 Almost AAPL US · Daily 9 Low-9 — 13 0700.HK HK · Daily 7 High — 13 600519 CN · Daily 9 High-9 13 13 Structure sketch · not a live screenshot Why add NineRadar if your broker already shows 9? The 9 is easy to find. The scarce thing is seeing who finished after the close, an honest reset, and a replay that only scores finished pairs. Typical trading apps vs NineRadar Paint 9 on the one chart you already opened. Finding 9 After the close, a list of who finished 9 or 13. One market, one symbol at a time. Markets US, HK, A-shares, and Korea on one list. The number appears; the story ends. Replay Replay only finished pairs: a low-9 waits for the next high-9. Unfinished 9s do not score. Alerts sit next to ads, shouts, and picks. Alerts A lock-screen alert. No ads. No picks. History stays on this phone. What you open after the close Free is the 9s on your list. Pro sees the whole close, the 13, and lock-screen alerts. Today Who finished it today When the session is in, the list shows finished low-9, high-9, and 13. You do not flip charts to hunt the number. Watchlist Names you already follow Free keeps eight names. Today can stay on that list. The full after-close list is Pro. Backtest Only finished pairs A win waits for the opposite 9. A low-9 counts if the next high-9 closes higher. History, not a ranking of stocks to buy. You Lock-screen notes Pro can push the close — and 60/120-minute counts — to the lock screen. Your history stays on this phone. How the 9 and the 13 are counted How the count works. The app lists who finished after the close — not another line on the chart. What is a TD Sequential 9? Nine closes versus four bars back. Labels start at 6. Fail 9 and 1–8 vanish. What is the TD Sequential 13? Countdown after a finished 9. It completes less often. An unfinished 13 can cancel. Low-9, high-9, Perfect, TDST The names on the list, and what they are not. Notes from a real close Evenings after the close, and the next morning. A Tongdaxin 9 that vanished, an empty 13 list, a meeting that will not say buy. The 7s fell off the candles I used to think the terminal was crashing. The 7 had been sitting under the bar since lunch. After one ugly close it was gone, and so were 1 through 6. I re-added the overlay twice. I read the tape. I did not read a buy list. We have twelve minutes. If I spend them explaining DeMark I get cut off. If I spend them pitching I get a compliance look. So I read names. “低9 了，明天低开就干” is not the definition The screenshot had a teal 9 under the bar and a caption that would not survive a compliance officer. I used to argue. Then I muted. Then I left. Read the notes Look up a stock after the close Open a name you already follow — Apple, Tencent, 茅台. See whether the daily 9 or 13 finished after that market’s close. Not a ranking. Find a stock Common questions What is a TD Sequential 9 (the “magic nine”)? Nine consecutive closes above or below the close four bars earlier. That prints a high-9 or a low-9. Chinese markets often call it 神奇九转. It is a count, not a trade order. If my broker already paints 9, why NineRadar? A quote app marks 9 on the symbol you opened. NineRadar lists who finished 9 or 13 after the close across US, HK, A-shares, and Korea, then scores only finished pairs. What is the difference between a low-9 and a high-9? A low"
